cked by robots.txt, no primary source found, so omitted; earlier rounds (2008 seed, 2018-2021) not evidenced. DOE HALEU allocation, Wyoming state money and DOE LPO: nothing evidenced (web search budget exhausted, energy.gov ARDP program page and terrapower.com/wyoming render without content); DOE LPO has no TerraPower loan in USAspending loan search (probe 2a20911efb92). Pennsylvania $10M grant is to the affiliate TerraPower Isotopes, stated by the state secretary, grant date unknown. VERIFIER: that event was REMOVED: the recipient is TerraPower Isotopes (TPI), a separate legal entity, and the source (snapshot 8b75270ea3b0, 2026-05-06, \"Our strategic $10 million grant helped to secure more than $450 million in private investment\") does not name TerraPower LLC as recipient or beneficiary. ARDP: the DOE 2020-10-13 $80M is now amount_kind duplicate of the USAspending DENE0009054 obligation ($1,696.9M obligated, $972.4M outlaid), which is the counted figure. US SFR OWNER LLC is treated as TerraPower's ARDP project entity because DOE names TerraPower LLC as the ARDP awardee, the award is under the ARDP FOA DE-FOA-0002271, and the recipient address (15800 Northup Way, Bellevue WA) is TerraPower's headquarters; USAspending gives no parent and the ownership of US SFR OWNER LLC is not evidenced (co-owners, if any, unknown). Meta release says Meta \"will provide funding\" for deployment but states no amount; recorded as agreement, not funding.\n","org":{"aliases":[],"country":"US","external_ids":{"cik":null,"companies_house":null,"lei":null,"pic":null,"ror":null,"siren":null,"uei":null,"wikidata":null},"hq_city":"Bellevue","id":"terrapower","kind":"company","lat":null,"legal_names":[],"logo":null,"lon":null,"name":"TerraPower LLC","parent_id":null,"website":"https://www.terrapower.com"},"totals":{"approx":false,"ceiling":0.0,"debt":0.0,"disbursed":975057397.27,"equity":1480000000.0,"obligated":1699903044.86,"public":1699903044.86,"total":3179903044.8599997,"undisclosed":1}}